gatelist.mjs --selftest — same-door known-bad corpus (10 plant(s))
DOOR: each plant enters as FILE BYTES in a copied real tree at the file(s) named below —
      the same file the real defect would ship in. The tool then runs WHOLE from that
      copy (cwd = copy root): readFileSync, the import graph, serve.mjs and any browser
      boot all read the planted bytes. Nothing is handed to an inner function directly.
      A plant carrying `prep` runs that command in the copy first, so a two-stage
      content door (spreadsheet -> content-build -> generated module) is travelled whole.
      Revert = the copy is discarded; the real tree is never edited.
      VERDICTS: CAUGHT = failed by its own named red · UNCAUGHT = tool stayed green
                (blind check, or the plant's premise moved) · RED-FOR-WRONG-REASON =
                failed by some OTHER red · RED-NOT-EXIT = red printed, exit still 0 ·
                DRIFTED = the find-string is gone, so the plant never armed at all.
